## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; capability decides)
- **G-1 delta and no-loosening (C1).** A path beyond the two, a byte of a product file, the b616 file, `support.ts`, a package, lock or config file = **Blocker**; any removed line beyond the five of FACTS, any other line of the 0021 block changed = **Major, class (e)**; a changed assertion of an old row or of `FIXTURES` = **Major, class (c)**; a person's name, real customer name, secret or decision-card slug in an added line or the message = **Blocker**; a second commit on top of `635fcdc3` or a moved head = STOP; a ticket key or work number in an added DEPLOY.md line = **Minor** (the test path in the pin paragraph is a Note); non-ASCII in the round-2 added lines = **Major**.
- **G-2 the words (C2, C3).** A sentence or row of `### Proven on` that says or implies the check was run on `pc-b114r` (including an ambiguous pointer a reader could take that way) = **Major, class (f)**; the count at the proof commit showing the check present = **Major, class (f)**; a new DEPLOY.md sentence no transcript of yours backs, or any claim about the demo VM = **Major, class (d)/(f)**; a "pins" claim with no row, or "Nothing else in the command is pinned." false = **Major, class (f)**; a sentence made false elsewhere in `DEPLOY.md` by the new text = **Major**; a loose-but-harmless pointer (row 250) = **Minor**; the six unchanged "Nothing pins Route B's command." sentences = a decision for Tuesday, **Note**.
- **G-3 the rows (C4).** A defect that breaks what a row's title says and stays green under all 10 rows = **Major, class (c)/(g)**; a row red for a reason other than its named one = **Major, class (c)**; M17, M18, E-move not red on E, M24, M25 not red on S, M29 not red on S, P1-P4 not red on P, or any of M17 M18 M24 M25 red under the ROUND-1 test = **Major, class (c)** (the last: the new rows are not what kills it; a claim that is only a number = Minor); M30 or M35 green = **Minor** when the pin paragraph claims MEANING ("says to stop", "names the check as not part of the run") by word pins, **Note** when it claims words; an unclaimed row that pins a document property = **Minor**, an unclaimed control row = **Note**; M32 green is the paragraph's point (Note, record it); a revert that turns more or fewer rows red than the builder claimed = **Minor** (name them) unless a named row is lost, then Major; a brittle extractor (an unrelated prose line breaks the test) or a `TMPDIR` dependence = **Note**; the builder's claim your run contradicts = **Major** if it hides a defect, **Minor** if only a number.
- **G-4 the scanner (C5).** The scanner flags the block, or a check line is not SEEN = **Major**; the scratch controls do not fire = the run is DEAD (say so, NOT TESTED); the range gap = **Note** (scanner lane, not this PR).
- **G-5 stability, CI, CodeQL (C6, C7).** A whole-suite red you reproduce twice = **Major**; the file other than 10 of 10, or the group other than round-1 head + 0 files + 3 tests (= main + 1 file + 10 tests), without a reason = a finding at the severity of its cause; names lost or added other than 0 / 3 = **Major**; lint/format/typecheck non-zero on the head = **Major** (format:check covers `DEPLOY.md`); a load-only red = artefact (record both runs); a failing check-run on the head or merge result = **Major**; `in_progress` at the verdict = `CI pending: <names>`, at most GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS; an open alert on the PR ref or merge ref = **Blocker** and a STOP; a textual conflict = **Major**; a path shared with another open PR or live lane = **Major**; a missing PRIOR WORK = returned. **Always Note:** the author field, dependabot's vulnerabilities line, the squash artefact (the PR title becomes the squash subject), the unreplaced STATUS placeholders, container-start count over budget.
- **G-6 the verdict follows the table, and the cap (round 2 of 2).** Any Blocker, or any Major = `NO GO (round 2 of 2)`: the class ENDS for this builder; FOR TUESDAY then carries the CLOSED list (with cells), the RESIDUE as ticket text with the tester's cells attached (B779-2 among it, as already ticketed), and the fact that a third round needs the product owner's word on a card (`model-routing.md:111`). Notes and Minors only = `GO` or `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS` (list the Deferred rows and every Minor; decisions in FOR TUESDAY). Add ` (conditional: <reason>)` for any required check not run; `CI pending` is always conditional. CodeQL is scanned on the head (the PR exists): the ceiling is not lowered for lack of a scan unless a run is missing or pending.

## LOAD (binding; Composer docker route)
8 cores shared with other projects' seats (load1 read **9.47 at 05:46**: the HPSM-POC seats are live and the builder may still run jobs). Heavy = `docker build`, any database-test container, the unit chain, any vitest over more than one file, the 50-MB-style and 200-run loops (none required this round), the `packages/db` group. **Start a heavy job only while `uptime` load1 is below 7 at two reads 4 s apart** (not independent reads: say so), recorded beside the result; at or over, poll every 20 s, log each wait, do light work meanwhile (C1, C2(c), the clone, writing instruments, C7 polls). **One heavy job of yours at a time**, behind `<project>/.tools/b787/lock` (copied `heavy.sh`; released by MOVE to `.tools/b787/quarantine/locks/`, never `rmdir`) and the cross-seat `ps` gate. A MOVING heartbeat (counter plus `date`) to `.tools/b787/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job. A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` on a pattern in its own command line (wait on a recorded PID, `wait $!`, or a done-marker file). Every command gets its input or none (`/dev/null`). NO artificial load. Build `pc-b787-node:head` once from the head's tree: `docker build --pull=false --progress=plain -f <tree>/docker/Dockerfile --target ci -t pc-b787-node:head <tree>` (an ABSOLUTE `-f`; `npm ci` must be CACHED); record node, npm, vitest, tsc, prettier, eslint, `bash --version`, `tail --version`, `grep --version` of the image (RELAYED: node v22.23.2, npm 10.9.8, vitest 5.0.0, tsc 5.9.3, GNU bash 5.2.15, `tail` 9.1, `grep` 3.8). Budget (write it at Step 0, about 20): three `packages/db` group runs (main, round-1 head, head) and the b616 file alone = 4 database starts, the smoke 0-1, node-only starts: file x3, rows alone, TZ, shuffle, TMPDIR, main-DEPLOY, round-1-DEPLOY, round-1 test (about 5), the mutant batch (1-2, one container, `--network none`, each mutant's DEPLOY.md and test copied over `/repo`), scanner (1-2), unit chain 1, typecheck 1. Remove ONLY your own `pc-b787-*` containers, networks and anonymous postgres volumes, by exact name.

