Datasec / Security Composer only; if any output shows another client's material, stop and disclose its shape. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra, Graph, ssh. **No HTTP to any hosted or production host or the demo site** (the demo VM's tools and a real restore are NOT TESTED by design; Route B is never run against anything but files and your own throwaway container). Never `docker exec`/`stop`/`rm`/`logs` against a container you did not create (the copied `dbtest.sh` execs into the database container it created itself). Network: your one in-clone `git fetch`, `gh api -X GET` under the project `GH_CONFIG_DIR`, nothing else; `gh run rerun`, `gh workflow run` and any POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE are forbidden; never dismiss an alert. Git in the project repo `2_Project_Files`: READ verbs only (`--no-optional-locks`: ls-remote, log, show, diff, cat-file, ls-tree, rev-parse, rev-list, merge-base, grep, config --get); clone, fetch, worktree add, merge-tree only inside `.tools/b787/repo` and `.tools/wt-b787-*`. **HP-NDA hold:** never open `HP Reporting and Docs/`, any SOW, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/` contents or `inbound/` folders. **The unit step's Essential Eight SOW text input is passed ONLY as a read-only bind mount into a `--network none` container, at the path the copied `unit.sh` already names (`PC_E8_SOW_TEXT`); stat it with `[ -f ]`; never open, print, grep, hash or quote it.** The Stamp slot "Stamped by" records Tuesday's `Q-2` answer; no answer reads NO, the bind mount is not made, and the unit rows that need the SOW text are NOT TESTED (the other unit steps still run). No decision-queue tool, scoreboard, Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool. Secrets only as environment; never open `4_Credentials/.env` except the NAME test, never `3_Access_Keys/`. **Never delete** (`rm`, `branch -D`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `prune`): quarantine to `.tools/b787/quarantine/`. **Never `cd`**; absolute single-quoted paths (they hold a space and `!`); write `${VAR}:path`; no unquoted word starting with `=`; no unquoted `$VAR` holding a command with spaces; multi-step chains under `bash -c` or a quoted-heredoc script; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `python3 -I` for anything reading a file you did not write; read your scripts back and scan for non-ASCII (a script that must carry U+2026 builds it at run time from `0xE2 0x80 0xA6`). Scratch changes (planted rows, swaps, cut files) live ONLY in `wt-b787-mut`, `wt-b787-probe`, `.tools/b787/scratch/` and the throwaway test database; never in a committed file. Synthetic data only. No person's name in any id, file or STATUS (say "the product owner"; do not quote git author fields), no card slug, clock from `date`. Nothing to any human. **STANDING LINES:** PRIOR-WORK CHECK (your STATUS carries a PRIOR WORK section naming what you read of the builder lane and the round-1 gate and what you reuse; a READY-class verdict without one is returned); no message to any human; Jira writes none; never delete (quarantine). **RESUME at about 80% of context or at the hard stop:** write `PROGRESS` and `RESUME` sections (each check done/partial/not started with evidence paths; next commands; every scratch tree with its restore proof; lock released), stop your processes and containers, end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` with the one question "continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?". **Usage pause:** if your session ends at the account's weekly limit, that is the platform, not a STOP; on resume re-read your own STATUS last line, re-pin main, the head and any checks, release or reclaim any lock you held by your own rule, and carry on against the hard stop Tuesday names.

